.\" man/man3/TreeSitter::Predicate.3cr
.\" Generated by scripts/man.cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "TreeSitter::Predicate" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "treesitter 0.1.0" "treesitter API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
TreeSitter::Predicate \- A text test on a query pattern, checked against the captured nodes\(aq text before a match is reported: \fB\%#eq?\fR, \fB\%#match?\fR, \fB\%#any\-of?\fR, their \fB\%not\-\fR forms and the \fB\%vim\-\fR and \fB\%lua\-\fR spellings of \fB\%#match?\fR.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "treesitter"\fR
.sp
\fBstruct TreeSitter::Predicate\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A text test on a query pattern, checked against the captured nodes\(aq text before a match is reported: \fB\%#eq?\fR,
\fB\%#match?\fR, \fB\%#any\-of?\fR, their \fB\%not\-\fR forms and the \fB\%vim\-\fR and \fB\%lua\-\fR spellings of \fB\%#match?\fR. Directives (\fB\%#set!\fR)
and unknown predicates are skipped, so the pattern matches as if they were absent; \fB\%Query#properties\fR reads \fB\%#set!\fR.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBLUA_CLASSES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
LUA_CLASSES = {
  \(aqa\(aq => "A\-Za\-z",
  \(aqc\(aq => "\e\ex00\-\e\ex1f\e\ex7f",
  \(aqd\(aq => "0\-9",
  \(aqg\(aq => "!\-\(ti",
  \(aql\(aq => "a\-z",
  \(aqp\(aq => "!\-/:\-@\e\e[\-\(ga{\-\(ti",
  \(aqs\(aq => "\e\es",
  \(aqu\(aq => "A\-Z",
  \(aqw\(aq => "A\-Za\-z0\-9",
  \(aqx\(aq => "0\-9A\-Fa\-f",
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Lua character class letter \[u2192] the regular expression range it stands for (uppercase negates).
.RE
.TP 4
\fBSET = "set!"\fR
Directive that sets a pattern property.
.TP 4
\fBTESTS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
TESTS = {
  "eq?" => {Test::Eq, false, false},
  "not\-eq?" => {Test::Eq, true, false},
  "match?" => {Test::Match, false, false},
  "not\-match?" => {Test::Match, true, false},
  "vim\-match?" => {Test::Match, false, false},
  "not\-vim\-match?" => {Test::Match, true, false},
  "lua\-match?" => {Test::Match, false, true},
  "not\-lua\-match?" => {Test::Match, true, true},
  "any\-of?" => {Test::AnyOf, false, false},
  "not\-any\-of?" => {Test::AnyOf, true, false},
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Predicate name \[u2192] \fB\%{test, \%negated, \%Lua \%pattern}\fR.
.RE
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(test : Test, negated : Bool, capture : Int32, other : Int32 | Nil, values : Array(String), regex : Regex | Nil)\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.list(query : Pointer(Void), pattern : Int32) : Array(Predicate)\fR
The predicates of \fIpattern\fR in the query at \fIquery\fR, in source order.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.lua(pattern : String) : String\fR
A regular expression for the Lua pattern \fIpattern\fR: \fB\%%\fR classes become ranges and \fB\%\-\fR outside a set becomes a
lazy \fB\%*?\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.properties(query : Pointer(Void), pattern : Int32) : Hash(String, String)\fR
The \fB\%#set!\fR properties of \fIpattern\fR in the query at \fIquery\fR: key \[u2192] value (\fB\%""\fR when the directive gives none).
A capture operand (\fB\%#set! \%@x \%key \%value\fR) is skipped.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef capture : Int32\fR
Capture id whose text is tested.
.TP 4
\fBdef negated? : Bool\fR
Whether the result is inverted.
.TP 4
\fBdef other : Int32 | Nil\fR
Capture id compared against, for \fB\%#eq?\fR between two captures.
.TP 4
\fBdef regex : Regex | Nil\fR
Compiled pattern of a \fB\%Match\fR test.
.TP 4
\fBdef satisfied?(captures : Slice(LibTreeSitter::QueryCapture), tree : Tree, source : Source) : Bool\fR
Whether the match whose \fIcaptures\fR came from \fItree\fR passes this test, reading text from \fIsource\fR. A capture
absent from the match passes.
.TP 4
\fBdef test : Test\fR
The comparison.
.TP 4
\fBdef values : Array(String)\fR
String operands.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/tree_sitter/predicate.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "TreeSitter" (3cr),
.BR "TreeSitter::Match" (3cr),
.BR "TreeSitter::Predicate::Test" (3cr),
